tags: event

= KPD Party Conference

Now is the KPD's national party conference, where we will choose our new leadership. The shadow of the Wittorf Affair hangs over it. On one hand are the hardline supporters of Thälmann, who support a "social fascist" policy that places the SPD as equivalent to the Nazis. On the other hand is the "Conciliator" faction, who support a more cooperative policy towards the SPD.

Stalin and the Comintern is heavily favoring Thälmann despite his coverup during the Wittorf Afair.

- @conciliator_success
- @conciliator_fail


@conciliator_success
title: The Conciliators are the new leadership of the KPD.
choose-if: comintern_influence <= 15 
unavailable-subtitle:  The Comintern has vetoed this action.
on-arrival: kpd_party_leader = "Conciliators"; communist_coalition += 3; spd_relation += 10
achievement: versohnler

With our support, the Conciliators have won the leadership contest! The new leadership is a group of Conciliators, including Arthur Ewert, Hugo Eberlein, and Ernst Meyer. Thälmann remains, but with reduced influence. Cooperation with the SPD  seems to be a more real possibility.


@conciliator_fail
title: Thälmann retains his leadership position.
on-arrival: expel_thalmann = 0; party_purged = 1; n_advisors -= 1 if zetkin_advisor == 1; zetkin_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if brandler_advisor == 1; brandler_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if thalheimer_advisor == 1; thalheimer_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if frolich_advisor == 1; frolich_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if meyer_advisor == 1; meyer_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if eberlein_advisor == 1; eberlein_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if ewert_advisor == 1; ewert_advisor = 0

The Comintern and our party leaders let Thälmann keep his leadership position. He quickly moves to consolidate absolute leadership, expelling or exiling his opponents.
